import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
s = open(p, encoding="utf-8", newline="").read()
nl = "\r\n" if "\r\n" in s else "\n"
anchor = "- **E4a DECISIONS ON A POSSIBLY DEGENERATE GROUP RESIDUAL"
assert s.count(anchor) == 1
new = ("- **GQ2's ONE BUILD (2026-10-20; the reviewer 17:34): the stall reads the trend, an unreadable frame holds the series, a held routable hypothesis acts first, a clock is not a subject.** "
       "THE TREND (TETHER_GOAL_HYPOTHESES): a held hypothesis keeps its own readings (from the cycle it was held); it ends \"stalled\" (by: trend) when, on every subject, MIN_REPEAT + 1 consecutive readings set no new low against the lowest before them (the reading at hold included) -- the selector's shrink test with the opposite sign; the gap budget is only the ceiling (by: ceiling). OFF: the old rule (at the budget, ended if no reading below r0). "
       "(a) THE HOLD (TETHER_ARRIVAL): note_goals' operand-unreadable exit on a slot that has a series HOLDS it (no append, no pop); every other None exit pops as before. The held cycles are counted on the hypothesis (held_unreadable on its end row, beside reads_n). The o1.rem_col flicker on sp80 (17:31, the operand readable on 6 of 15 steps) is NAMED here and not chased. "
       "(b) THE ORDER (TETHER_GOAL_HYPOTHESES): in choose, after the held-routine branch and the routine attempt, a held hypothesis that the selector chose and that has a route (_goal_split's probe) acts through _goal_split (by discriminate:goal) before the starved-contact probe, the bored probe, the exit choice and System 0; with no route the branches run as before. The hypothesis's end row carries acted (the count of each exit that acted while it was held). "
       "(3) THE CLOCK (TETHER_GOAL_HYPOTHESES): _self_moving(slot) reads the agent's own delta table -- the slot moved on EVERY press of EVERY surfaced action, by the same mean delta, not zero -- and _hyp_propose refuses it as a subject (\"self-moving subject\"); it may still be an operand. An action never taken, or one press that left the slot still, leaves the dependence open (accepted). THE EXISTING READERS: GQ2's own movable-subject test (a non-derived slot) reads membership only, so it was blind to a clock -- (3) sits beside it, not in it. Agency.contingent() (the respell path's reader) is NOT blind (it needs an action that always moves and one that never does), but it is too strict for a subject (a slot moved +1 by one action and -1 by another is steerable and not contingent), so it was not reused and not widened. "
       "test_hyp_trend (one process, the arm toggled at the call): T1 flat readings ON end stalled by trend, OFF held inside the budget, falling readings ON held; T2 one operand-unreadable frame ON keeps the series at 2 with held_unreadable 1, OFF restarts it (0); T3 System 0 forced active, ON the route ('down') is taken by discriminate:goal, OFF System 0 acts ('left'); T4 a planted -2-every-action o0.col is refused ON (15 candidates refused as self-moving, open 170) and accepted OFF (0, open 180); o0.row moved only under the last action is not self-moving." + nl)
s = s.replace(anchor, new + anchor)
open(p, "w", encoding="utf-8", newline="").write(s)
print("ok", nl == "\r\n")
